Included in bls-4.0.sqlite
  bls_foods            7,140 records
    of which flagged   2,992 as ingredient_preferred — the raw/base INGREDIENT subset, as
                       opposed to prepared menu components and cooking-state variants. The
                       flag comes from ingredient-codes-2992.txt in this directory; that
                       file documents how the selection was made and why the flag is used
                       only by the degraded-mode matching policy.

  There is exactly ONE runtime BLS database. The flag marks rows within it; it does not
  describe a second, smaller database.

What was transformed
  Only the fields this service needs are imported: BLS code, German name, English name and
  11 nutrient columns, out of the full 418-column / 138-nutrient official export.

  Every stored number is either a verbatim BLS 4.0 figure or null — null exactly where BLS
  itself reports no value. Sodium and cholesterol are divided by 1000 (mg -> g) so units
  match every other provider. Nothing is estimated, averaged, interpolated or hand-authored.

Regeneration
      python3 scripts/import_bls.py BLS_4_0_Daten_2025_DE.xlsx

  The importer reproduces this attribution in its own header and writes it into bls_meta.
